---
description: Frontend uses develop for testing; backend uses staging—commit frontend to develop unless going live
alwaysApply: true
---

# Environments (frontend vs backend)

- **Backend**: **staging** is the testing/preview deployment (Railway or equivalent). Point `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` / BFF at the **staging** backend URL when testing the frontend against non-production APIs.
- **Frontend (this repo)**: **`develop`** is the branch for frontend preview/staging builds. Naming is intentional: backend “staging” ≠ frontend branch name.

# Test branch workflow (frontend only)

- **Test branch**: `develop` — all routine commits and pushes for this repo target **`develop`** until the user says otherwise.
  - Checkout `develop` before committing when working on staging/preview.
  - Push with: `git push origin develop` (or `git push -u origin develop` once).
- **Production**: `main` is for **live** frontend; do not commit or push to `main` unless the user explicitly asks to go live or merge/promote to production.
- If the user says to stop using `develop` or to work on `main` again, remove or ignore this rule.
